  "notes": [
    "This inventory records technical boundaries, not prices, commercial editions or universal cross-product bundle rights.",
    "A subsequent public product operation requires its own grant; DTO creation and metadata access do not imply renderer permission.",
    "Code, Viewer, PDF Designer and all eight Report Designer providers now enforce native admission. Cross-product and protected-package acceptance remain separate.",
    "Report detection and generic package utilities do not grant conversion rights; auto is resolved to a concrete canonical provider before resource merging and conversion. Standalone DevExpress resource parsing needs DevExpress rights; shared in-operation RESX handling uses only the selected report provider grant.",
    "Nutrient Designer alone may enter a private DesignerPdfImport continuation and internal Viewer mapping for its source PDF. It cannot invoke public Importer, Viewer or PDF operations without fresh rights.",
    "PDF Code preview starts independently licensed public PDF creation/serialization; Code admission reserves no future PDF rights. Spreadsheet preview is text-to-HTML replay, not workbook processing.",
    "Only existing purpose-bound private byte dependencies avoid an additional public PDF grant. No new private PDF rights are introduced."
  ]
